      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues exceed analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹21.93 (up from ₹18.22 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹8.88b (up 14% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹728.7m (up 20% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 8.2% (up from 7.8% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 1.3%. Earnings per share (EPS) also surpassed analyst estimates by 1.5%. Revenue is forecast to grow 12% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 13% growth forecast for the Packaging industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 5% per year but the company’s share price has fallen by 15% per year, which means it is performing significantly worse than earnings.",
